      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "What are the biggest mistakes when buying a treadmill?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "The costliest are comparing motors on peak rather than continuous horsepower, buying a deck too short for the longest stride in the house, ignoring ceiling height and the clearance behind the belt, and not measuring the delivery route. Close behind are too little weight-capacity headroom, unpriced subscription costs, and a warranty with no labour cover.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "What should I avoid when buying a treadmill?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Avoid machines that only quote peak horsepower, decks shorter than your stride needs at your fastest pace, a weight capacity that only just covers the heaviest user, and warranties that cover parts but not labour. Also avoid ordering before you have measured the room, the ceiling and every doorway and stair turn on the way in.",
