          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Is it a mistake to buy a folding treadmill?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Not if you will genuinely fold it. Folding is valuable in a room that has to serve another purpose. But folding frames are usually less rigid than fixed ones at the same price, the hinge is a wear point, and a folded machine still stands five to six feet tall. If it will stay down permanently, a non-folding machine is usually the better buy.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "How much ceiling height do I need for a treadmill?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Add your height, the deck height of the machine and at least 12 inches of head clearance. Deck heights range from about 5 inches on a walking pad to 12 inches or more on a cushioned treadmill, so a 6-foot runner on a typical machine can need a ceiling of around 7 foot 10. Incline raises the front further.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Should I buy a treadmill without trying it first?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Many people do, and it usually works out, but it makes the return policy the real test. Before ordering, confirm the return window, whether it still applies once assembled, who pays for collection and whether there is a restocking fee. If you can, try a comparable deck and console at a store or gym at the speeds you will actually use.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Do I need a treadmill mat on carpet?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Almost always. On bare carpet a treadmill draws fibre and dust into the motor compartment through its air intake, sits less stably, and leaves permanent crush marks. A proper treadmill mat, larger than the machine's footprint, addresses all three. On hard floors a mat is more often optional, though it still protects the floor.",
          },
        },
      ],
    },
    {
