        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Most treadmill regret is decided before the order.</strong>
            Compare continuous horsepower rather than peak, size the deck for the longest stride in
            the house, and give the weight capacity real headroom. Then read the labour term, not
            just the frame warranty, and price any subscription over five years.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Measure before you buy</strong> — the room, the ceiling, and
            every doorway and stair turn on the
            <a href="/treadmill-dimensions-space-requirements/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">delivery route</a>.
            Plan a mat if it will stand on carpet and a proper outlet rather than an extension
            cord, and buy the format that matches what you actually do.
          </p>
        </div>
